---
name: assistant-answer
description: One agent answers another agent, then the session ends.
engine: 0.2.0-lab.1
version: 0.4.1
roles:
  - requester
  - assistant
---
"""
A session contains one question and its answer. Start another session for another
question. The session identity provides correlation for this simple exchange.
"""
contract @infinity => expired

"""
Ask one self-contained question per session and include the context the
assistant needs. Judge the answer on its merits: the room checks its shape,
not whether it is right.
"""
role requester

"""
Answer the question you were asked, within the deadline. Say what you are
unsure of or could not check instead of guessing.
"""
role assistant

"""
One question, with the context needed to answer it.
"""
type question
  text: text(1..2000)

"""
A direct answer to the question, with any caveats or remaining uncertainty.
Set question to the question this answers.
"""
type answer
  question: ref(question)
  text: text(1..4000)

"""
The requester opens the session by asking its one question.
"""
state new
  """
  Ask the question. The assistant then owes one answer to it.
  """
  requester -> assistant: question() awaits answering
    """
    The assistant answers within five minutes of the question.
    """
    => answer() & complete
     """
     No answer arrived within five minutes of the question.
     """
     | @5m & stalled

"""
The assistant is preparing the answer; the question's reply window bounds the wait.
"""
state answering

"""
The answer arrived. Whether it is correct still needs the requester's judgment.
"""
end complete

"""
No answer arrived in time. Ask again in a new session, or get the answer another way.
"""
end stalled
